# Wave W17-P (Copperbore Tunnel): bore wall — chalk-X inspection wall: dressed brown-grey strata bands carrying the tunnelers’ inspection culture in the art itself — a warm lamp band running at shoulder height where the bore’s lamps hang, and pale chalk flecks struck through it like the crews’ X-marks (design: inspection lamps and X-marks drawn in the wall kind’s art, art layer only). Copperbore’s own wall — split from Scorch Path’s heat-darkened ember bands by the lamp band (worked light, not firelight) and from Comet Falls’ star seam by register: chalk and lamplight, not fallen sky.
PIX borewall 16 16
